{"abstract":"This article measures and explains cost risk for IT projects compared with 22 other project types. The null hypothesis is that IT projects are not different from other projects in terms of cost risk. The thesis is falsified. IT cost risk is found to be uniquely more risky than other project types. First, we review four extant explanations of high IT cost risk: immaturity, intangibility, goal ambiguity, and stakeholder resistance. Second, we describe data to measure cost risk across 23 project types, including IT. Third, we fit theoretical distributions to the data and test for median and tail risk, showing that tail risk dominates, with IT cost risk having a fatter tail than any other project type. Fourth, we develop a taxonomy of risk based on the Pareto 1 tail parameter α, documenting that IT is uniquely risky as the only project type with α ≤ 1, indicating infinite mean and variance and, thus, infinite and unpredictable risk. Fifth, we return to the four extant explanations and conclude that, although our data do not prove the explanations, they also do not falsify them. Based on our data, we suggest two further explanations of cost risk: Bespokeness and “think-fast” decision-making, which we argue drive extreme risk and are typical of IT, with modularity and “think slow” as antidotes. Finally, we identify areas for further research.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Flyvbjerg, Bent","Budzier, Alexander","Aaen, Jon","Keil, Mark","Zottoli, Mariagrazia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-823168"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the uniqueness of it cost risk a cross group comparison of 000000000023 project types","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/87569728251340590","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-823168","ids":["aau-0e1909f1-9b9a-408b-8e10-aca67712b30c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-60F5182B4CED129C9F12998E87D96B36"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/87569728251340590","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Public Administration & Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bent","key":"flyvbjergpau","last":"Flyvbjerg","name":"Flyvbjerg, Bent","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"budzierpau","last":"Budzier","name":"Budzier, Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"keilpau","last":"Keil","name":"Keil, Mark","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mariagrazia","key":"zottolipau","last":"Zottoli","name":"Zottoli, Mariagrazia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/87569728251340590","issn":["19389507","87569728"],"issn_org":["87569728"],"journal":"Project Management Journal","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"e","title":"Project Management Journal"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["aau-0e1909f1-9b9a-408b-8e10-aca67712b30c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Uniqueness of IT Cost Risk: A Cross-Group Comparison of 23 Project Types","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-823168","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"As software grows in size and complexity, organizations increasingly apply tools to automatically assess software quality of information systems during development and maintenance. Software quality assessment tools (SWQAT) promise fast and actionable insights into the technical state of software through various quality characteristics, such as maintainability, reliability, or security. These tools have been used to support a wide variety of IT project management decisions related to system development, contract negotiations, project terminations, and even settling legal disputes between suppliers and clients. However, despite their rising importance, questions regarding how they function and how reliable they are to support decision-making have so far escaped scholarly attention. This paper conducts an evaluation of widely used SWQATs and analyzes how they rate the quality of software systems of varying sizes, functionalities, and programming languages. Our results reveal five key challenges for using SWQATs in IT projects. To address these challenges, we propose a design for tailorable SWQATs that allows for more conscious and prudent software quality assessments that better reflect the socio-technical aspect of software systems and the context-specific nature of software quality.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Aaen, Jon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730195"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Project control and monitoring","Software quality","information systems management tools","software quality assessment tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tools for monitoring software quality in information systems development and maintenance five key challenges and a design proposal","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.12821/ijispm120102","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730195","identifier":[{"id":"85189794450","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ce6096be-7169-4b94-9540-075b4aa62859"],"keyword":["information systems management tools","project control and monitoring","software quality","software quality assessment tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F909E08E82E61B2CA6ACD19E2EA7398E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103580697/ijispm-120102.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.12821/ijispm120102","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Danish Institute for IT Program Management","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"6b81fcf4-173e-4e8b-86d6-2c9e7b4320c6","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-ce6096be-7169-4b94-9540-075b4aa62859"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tools for monitoring software quality in information systems development and maintenance: five key challenges and a design proposal","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730195","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Digitalization is a core component of the green transition. Today’s focus is on quantifying and predicting the climate effects of digitalization through various life-cycle assessments and baseline scenario methodologies. Here we argue that this is a mistake. Most attempts at prediction are based on three implicit assumptions: (a) the digital carbon footprint can be quantified, (b) business-as-usual with episodic change leading to a new era of stability, and (c) investments in digitalization will be delivered within the cost, timeframe, and benefits described in their business cases. We problematize each assumption within the context of digitalization and argue that the digital carbon footprint is inherently unpredictable. We build on uncertainty literature to show that even if you cannot predict, you can still mitigate. On that basis, we propose to rethink practice on the digital carbon footprint from prediction to mitigation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gritsenko, Daria","Aaen, Jon","Flyvbjerg, Bent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747224"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Helsinki"],"keyword":["Climate change mitigation","Climate change policy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rethinking digitalization and climate don t predict mitigate","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44168-024-00127-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747224","ids":["itu-493b8bd6-df2f-4e6c-b415-4a8c76b2bb67"],"keyword":["Climate-change mitigation","Climate-change policy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E6BD75E0CDBD12BD7F49AC68A4541CA7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105511429/Rethinking_digitalization_and_climate.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44168-024-00127-z","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Danish Institute for IT Program Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daria","key":"gritsenkopau","last":"Gritsenko","name":"Gritsenko, Daria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"6b81fcf4-173e-4e8b-86d6-2c9e7b4320c6","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bent","key":"flyvbjergpau","last":"Flyvbjerg","locid":"598de448-af84-43c8-9147-6134a63c9b3c","name":"Flyvbjerg, Bent","orcid":"0000-0001-9093-770X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-493b8bd6-df2f-4e6c-b415-4a8c76b2bb67"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rethinking digitalization and climate: don’t predict, mitigate","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747224","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Public sector organizations increasingly engage in robotic innovation projects to assist or substitute for humans in service delivery. However, transitioning small-scale development projects into a large-scale context is a notoriously difficult task that often fails, with many promising robotic projects becoming lost in the diffusion 'chasm.' We investigate a failed robotic diffusion project to analyze what went wrong and what can be learned from it. Despite an increased interest in learning from public sector digitalization failure, little attention has been paid to how and why seemingly successful service robot initiatives fail to move beyond the pilot stage. We identify three types of explanations for diffusion failure using an in-depth case study of a service robot initiative in the Danish eldercare sector that had a high degree of management support and commitment from key stakeholders. Our analysis demonstrates how the failure was caused by interrelated and context-specific reasons regarding the lack of technological maturity of the service robot (technology-oriented explanations), inadequate problem-solution fit in the conceptual design (scope-oriented explanations), and misalignment between the robot company and public sector organization mindsets (competing logic-oriented explanations). We outline the lessons learned for public sector digitalization and discuss the paradox between the hype surrounding robot innovations and their slow diffusion.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon","Agger Nielsen, Jeppe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-071633"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Aaen, Jon"],"keyword":["Diffusion","Public Sector Digitalization","Service robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lost in the diffusion chasm lessons learned from a failed robot project in the public sector","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85127205522&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-071633","identifier":[{"id":"85127205522","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4a767a21-38d6-4024-9ed8-0417705620f3"],"keyword":["Public sector digitalization","diffusion","diffusion chasm","learning from failure","service robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7565C16FCEAF7412F62088141BA23430"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe Agger","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"31d251b9-30db-4478-8e0c-c49badda7112","name":"Agger Nielsen, Jeppe","name_org":"Nielsen, Jeppe Agger","orcid":"0000-0002-8675-326X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/ip-200286","issn":["15701255","18758754"],"issn_org":["15701255"],"issue":"1","journal":"Information Polity","pages":"3-20","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Information Polity","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127205522"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4a767a21-38d6-4024-9ed8-0417705620f3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Lost in the diffusion chasm : Lessons learned from a failed robot project in the public sector","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-071633","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Data are often vividly depicted as strategic assets that organisations can (re)use to create value for myriad purposes. However, the same qualities that make data so appreciated—that is, their volume, their value for a plurality of stakeholders and their indefinite reuse capacity—also have a dark side: data reuse can lead to deviant data use that undermines the legitimacy of data analytics initiatives. To investigate this dynamic, we build on the notion of data ecosystems and provide empirical evidence from a longitudinal, 15-year case study of the emergence, expansion and eventual collapse of a large-scale data analytics project—called DAMD—in the Danish health care sector. We demonstrate that data reuse in the evolving data ecosystem elicited a data reuse dark side that was so dominant that it eventually resulted in the project’s demise. We conceptualize the reuse dark side’s three major mechanisms as function creep, stakeholder creep and data creep. Based on these insights, we develop an empirically grounded Data Analytics Ecosystem Model that extends the current understanding of data ecosystems and provides a view of these ecosystems as having both a bright and a dark side.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon","Agger Nielsen, Jeppe","Carugati, Andrea"],"cuid":["S02-099.92-000329"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Aaen, Jon"],"keyword":["Dark side","Data analytics","Data ecosystems","Data reuse","Longitudinal case study"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the dark side of data ecosystems a longitudinal study of the damd project","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/326125430/Aaen_2022_The_dark_side_of_data_ecosystems.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-099.92-000329","identifier":[{"id":"000672206100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85110897955","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-063cec2c-d05c-4a47-a7f7-671579ba64f7","au-45796d25-d5e5-48ec-818d-19dba873edfb"],"keyword":["Data analytics","Patrick Mikalef, Aleš Popovic, Jenny Eriksson Lundström and Kieran Conboy","dark side","data ecosystems","data reuse","longitudinal case study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4681D547947D0DBC5A0304B82E87EA14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/326125430/Aaen_2022_The_dark_side_of_data_ecosystems.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe Agger","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"31d251b9-30db-4478-8e0c-c49badda7112","name":"Agger Nielsen, Jeppe","name_org":"Nielsen, Jeppe Agger","orcid":"0000-0002-8675-326X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrea","key":"carugatipau","last":"Carugati","locid":"80c2f800-45ce-4d91-9446-c3c5c6a7086c","name":"Carugati, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0003-4611-3513","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0960085x.2021.1947753","issn":["0960085X","14769344"],"issn_org":["0960085X"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Information Systems","pages":"288-312","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Information Systems","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85110897955"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-063cec2c-d05c-4a47-a7f7-671579ba64f7","au-45796d25-d5e5-48ec-818d-19dba873edfb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The dark side of data ecosystems : A longitudinal study of the DAMD project","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.92-000329","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094492"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Competing concerns","Digital innovation","Innovation management","Welfare technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"managing competing concerns in digital innovation examining welfare technology in denmark","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.54337/aau470866361","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094492","ids":["aau-993d663c-7bd9-4aae-a2a8-f09555906c54"],"keyword":["Competing concerns","Digital innovation","Innovation management","Welfare Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D959A3A2D18EE608B76911F44A30C95E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/549452745/phd_JA_SSH_e_pdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.54337/aau470866361","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.54337/aau470866361","issn":["27942694"],"pages":"209","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","series":"Ph.d.-serien for Det Humanistiske og Samfundsvidenskabelige fakultet, Aalborg Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-993d663c-7bd9-4aae-a2a8-f09555906c54"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Managing Competing Concerns in Digital Innovation : Examining Welfare Technology in Denmark","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094492","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Welfare technologies (WT) such as telecare, service robots, and other digital innovations for public sector service delivery are expected to improve and even radically transform health- and eldercare. However, despite political awareness and financial investments, many studies report promising inventions that fail to become implemented on a larger scale. Current research draws a fragmented and heterogeneous picture of this problem, with divergent implications for practice. This article reviews and discusses the extant literature to identify eight competing concerns central to how WT can become implemented on a large scale. By highlighting and contrasting practical and theoretical positions in this emerging and interdisciplinary research topic, the review contributes to understanding the complexities that managers and policy-makers must address to diffuse and sustain WT innovations from small to large scale.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-100541"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adoption and diffusion","Digital innovation","Systematic literature review","Welfare technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"competing concerns on emerging welfare technologies a review of eight prevailing debates in current literature","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/sjis/vol33/iss1/7/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-100541","identifier":[{"id":"85127434266","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ae0e580e-8332-424a-8806-e9e5d2fcfda5"],"keyword":["Adoption and diffusion","Digital innovation","Systematic literature review","Welfare technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D8B720F46329EF64F4743A09C9173AEB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09050167"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","pages":"193-234","publisher":"The IRIS Association (Information Systems Research in Scandinavia), the Scandinavian chapter of the Association for Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127434266"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ae0e580e-8332-424a-8806-e9e5d2fcfda5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Competing Concerns on Emerging Welfare Technologies : A review of eight prevailing debates in current literature","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-100541","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Emerging technologies, such as robots, virtual homecare, and sensor technologies, have considerable potentials to transform health- and eldercare. These so-called welfare technologies (WTs) are expected to increase the quality of services, empower citizens, improve working conditions for professionals, and reduce costs for care providers. However, as this transformation this involves both technological development and radical changes in how these services are organized, many promising WTs fail to advance beyond the pilot stage and create value on a large scale. This paper reports the results of a longitudinal case study of the emergence of a service robot in primary healthcare, from project launch to testing, development, and evaluation. Seeking new ways of organizing emerging technologies, nine Danish municipalities and a consortium of four private companies launched a collaborative project, aiming to develop and implement the use of a drug-dispensing robot for patients living at home. The analysis traces how project managers respond to competing concerns on innovation strategy, testing, coordination, and user mobilization and how these critical decisions shape the project’s trajectory. As such, the paper sheds new light on how to understand and manage competing concerns in the process of organizing emergent WTs.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-051758"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","end":"2019-08-14","place":"Tampere, fi","start":"2019-08-12","title":"IRIS","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Competing concerns","Innovation process","Longitudinal case study","Welfare technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organizing for emerging welfare technology launching a drug dispensing robot for independent living","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/iris2019/1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-051758","ids":["aau-05ec29f0-0757-46b9-93f9-dbecc34b9bb7"],"keyword":["competing concerns","healthcare robot","innovation process","longitudinal case study","welfare technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-29D228DEBE2A651B2607F71D092E3EE7"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18919863","23873353"],"issn_org":["18919863"],"issue":"10","journal":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","publisher":"Scandinavian Chapter of the Association for Information Systems (AIS) - Scandinavian IRIS","status":"p","title":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","title_org":"IRIS Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-05ec29f0-0757-46b9-93f9-dbecc34b9bb7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Organizing For Emerging Welfare Technology : Launching A Drug-Dispensing Robot For Independent Living","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-051758","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Welfare technologies (WT) such as telecare and service robots are expected to improve and even radically transform service delivery in health- and eldercare. Yet despite political awareness and financial investments, many studies report promising inventions that fail to become implemented on a larger scale. Current research draws a fragmented and heterogeneous picture of this problem, with divergent implications for practice. In this article, I review and discuss the extant literature and identify eight competing concerns that are central to how WT can become implemented on a large scale. By highlighting and contrasting practical and theoretical positions in this emerging and interdisciplinary research topic, I contribute conceptually to the understanding of the competing concerns in WT innovation that managers and policy-makers must balance in order to support the critical transition from small-scale invention to large-scale implementation.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon"],"cuid":["S02-089.64-822404"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-14","place":"Nokia, fi","start":"2019-08-11","title":"10th Scandinavian Conference on Information Systems, SCIS 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Aaen, Jon"],"keyword":["Adoption","Assistive technology","Diffusion","Innovation","Literature review","Upscaling","Welfare technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"competing concerns in welfare technology innovation a systematic literature review","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320777458/Competing_Concerns_in_Welfare_Technology_Innovation_A_Systematic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.64-822404","identifier":[{"id":"85138733657","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9a7d40eb-3932-483f-8f51-39377292a432","aau-9d29dd1f-63b1-4841-989f-dcdf163c109b"],"keyword":["Adoption","Assistive technology","Diffusion","Innovation","Literature review","Upscaling","Welfare technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-BF01C79EE7220A4B2856CAA5F0412468"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/scis2019/3/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320777458/Competing_Concerns_in_Welfare_Technology_Innovation_A_Systematic.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780578532127"],"publisher":"Association for Information Systems (AIS)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 10th Scandinavian Conference on Information Systems (SCIS2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9a7d40eb-3932-483f-8f51-39377292a432","aau-9d29dd1f-63b1-4841-989f-dcdf163c109b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Competing Concerns in Welfare Technology Innovation : A Systematic Literature Review","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.64-822404","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Velfærdsteknologidagsordenen indtager en væsentlig rolle i diskussion om det danske velfærdssamfund, navnlig på sundheds- og ældreområdet. Artiklen redegør for tendensen og ridser baggrunden op for den aktuelle interesse for velfærdsteknologi som teknologisk satsningsområde. Vi byder ind med en definition af paraplybegrebet velfærdsteknologi og viser, hvordan forhåbningerne til velfærdsteknologi afspejler fire sameksisterende perspektiver; et effektivitets-, empowerment-, medarbejder- og vækstperspektiv. Baseret på resultater fra telemedicinprojektet TeleCare Nord illustrerer vi, hvordan de fire velfærdsteknologiperspektiver udfolder sig i praksis, og vi diskuterer udfordringer forbundet med at realisere forhåbningerne til velfærdsteknologi.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon","Agger Nielsen, Jeppe","Elmholdt, Kasper Trolle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Telemedicin","Velfærdsteknologi"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000010 år med velfærdsteknologi strategi og praksis","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22439/sis.v33i3.5552","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094686","ids":["aau-99f402e2-32fb-49d9-9f5a-87f246f34610"],"keyword":["telemedicin","velfærdsteknologi"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-59182AC5CAA4BF841D8EF840D1C4DD0E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22439/sis.v33i3.5552","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rauli.cbs.dk/index.php/SiS/article/view/5552/6357","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"31d251b9-30db-4478-8e0c-c49badda7112","name":"Agger Nielsen, Jeppe","name_org":"Nielsen, Jeppe","orcid":"0000-0002-8675-326X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper Trolle","key":"elmholdtpau","last":"Elmholdt","locid":"52842045-d8fd-4f7c-b4a1-6c2510d690af","name":"Elmholdt, Kasper Trolle","orcid":"0000-0002-0325-5266","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.22439/sis.v33i3.5552","issn":["09008322"],"issue":"3","journal":"Samfundslederskab i Skandinavien","pages":"236-259","publisher":"DenOffentlige","status":"p","title":"Samfundslederskab i Skandinavien","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-99f402e2-32fb-49d9-9f5a-87f246f34610"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"10 år med velfærdsteknologi : Strategi og praksis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094686","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we investigate the unintended consequences of initiating a large data analytic (DA) initiative in healthcare. DA is promising in terms of aiding decision making both for healthcare decisions and administrative decisions. However, while the (re)use of large amounts of data has lots of potential, it also has a dark side in terms of privacy, ethics, and control. Through the analysis of a longitudinal case study (2003-2015) of the emergence, expansion, and collapse of a large-scale DA project in the Danish healthcare sector, we demonstrate how high expectations for DA caused a surge of stakeholders and features that ultimately resulted in the project’s demise. We call these surges stakeholder creep and function creep and theorize their emergence and consequences for DA in organizations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon","Agger Nielsen, Jeppe"],"cuid":["S02-085.71-001305"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIS","end":"2018-06-28","place":"Portsmouth, gb","start":"2018-06-23","title":"26th European Conference on Information Systems, ECIS 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Big data","Data analytics","Project management","Stakeholder"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the dark side of successful data intensive projects function creep and stakeholder creep","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/ecis2018_rp/191/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-085.71-001305","identifier":[{"id":"85061343569","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1953937c-dbef-439f-b83a-de8812955c56","aau-fcc0771d-245d-40d3-bd02-4ff67325c6d1"],"keyword":["Function Creep","Project Management","Stakeholder","Stakeholder Creep","big data","data analytics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-C7253264FD412E8027DB583FD2622485"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/ecis2018_rp/191/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jon","key":"aaenpau","last":"Aaen","locid":"3d81e322-04e5-4232-9352-9314d1576728","name":"Aaen, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-2176-4678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe Agger","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"31d251b9-30db-4478-8e0c-c49badda7112","name":"Agger Nielsen, Jeppe","name_org":"Nielsen, Jeppe Agger","orcid":"0000-0002-8675-326X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe","key":"aggernielsenpau","last":"Agger Nielsen","locid":"31d251b9-30db-4478-8e0c-c49badda7112","name":"Agger Nielsen, Jeppe","orcid":"0000-0002-8675-326X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000034"],"journal":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","paperid":"191","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems (ECIS)","volume":"2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1953937c-dbef-439f-b83a-de8812955c56","aau-fcc0771d-245d-40d3-bd02-4ff67325c6d1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Dark Side of Successful Data Intensive Projects : Function Creep And Stakeholder Creep","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.71-001305","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"New service robots are increasingly being adopted to improve and even radically transform and innovate (public) service delivery such as healthcare, eldercare, and education. Yet, organization-oriented research on how these new technologies impact people, processes, and services is very limited. In this paper, I argue for the importance of studying these issues from an (public) organization-oriented and information system research perspective. I review and discuss current literature on the major advances of robotics in welfare services as an emerging and interdisciplinary research topic, exploring the current state of the art and present a foundation to guide future research. Particular emphasis is given to organizational challenges concerning implementation and value realization.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Aaen, Jon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-111676"],"event":{"end":"2018-08-08","start":"2018-08-05","title":"IRIS/SCIS Conference 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robots in welfare services a systematic literature review","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-111676","ids":["aau-d4275d39-875f-4d75-8e9b-c6ad5d2172d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CE8194F69E40926D5196F5443E14D498"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanit